From: spark-ds41f <dev@local>
Subject: [PATCH] distributed: allow nccl-socket TP collectives (no RoCE, uint32 all_gather)

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm @ 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
  plus candidate-62 series (expected tree 8fc99ca7546c5c538f0fe64e7c82954f1d2d7ae0).
Rationale:
  1. CudaCommunicator unconditionally enabled sparknet RoCE on TP groups,
     preventing nccl-socket / Ethernet-only functional tests when RDMA cabling
     is absent. When NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1, leave use_roce_allreduce=False so PyNCCL
     handles TP collectives over TCP while keeping the fail-closed RoCE guard
     unchanged whenever IB/RoCE is enabled.
  2. TileLang's wo.py all-gathers packed uint32 scale factors across TP ranks;
     PyNCCL supports int32 rather than uint32, so view uint32 as int32 around
     pynccl_comm.all_gather (bit-identical raw byte gather).
Quality implications:
  None.
Tests:
  Verified zero-fuzz apply on spark-ds41f:1120; used by pp2-tp2-socket.json.
Upstream status:
  Local experiment patch for Ethernet-only functional verification.

--- a/vllm/distributed/device_communicators/cuda_communicator.py
+++ b/vllm/distributed/device_communicators/cuda_communicator.py
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project
 
 
+import os
 from typing import TYPE_CHECKING
 
 import torch
@@ -141,12 +142,15 @@
                     "VLLM_ENABLE_ROCE_ALLREDUCE selected B12X's RoCE collectives, "
                     "which are gone; sparknet's one-shot collectives are always on"
                 )
-            if not use_custom_allreduce:
-                raise ValueError(
-                    "sparknet's one-shot collectives need custom all-reduce"
-                )
-            use_roce_allreduce = True
-            use_flashinfer_allreduce = False
+            if os.environ.get("NCCL_IB_DISABLE") == "1":
+                use_roce_allreduce = False
+            else:
+                if not use_custom_allreduce:
+                    raise ValueError(
+                        "sparknet's one-shot collectives need custom all-reduce"
+                    )
+                use_roce_allreduce = True
+                use_flashinfer_allreduce = False
 
         self.use_custom_allreduce = use_custom_allreduce
         self.use_torch_symm_mem = use_torch_symm_mem
@@ -676,7 +680,13 @@
         output_tensor = torch.empty(
             output_size, dtype=input_.dtype, device=input_.device
         )
-        pynccl_comm.all_gather(output_tensor, input_.contiguous())
+        if input_.dtype == torch.uint32:
+            pynccl_comm.all_gather(
+                output_tensor.view(torch.int32),
+                input_.contiguous().view(torch.int32),
+            )
+        else:
+            pynccl_comm.all_gather(output_tensor, input_.contiguous())
         if dim > 0 and dim == input_.dim() - 1:
             # The rank-major shards side by side in one TileLang launch, not
             # torch's movedim and reshape copy.
